    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d484">

                <pb facs="0572" n="474" sameAs="frus:frus1932v04/pg474"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">793.94/3918: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Secretary of State to the Minister in China
                        (Johnson)</hi></head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1932-02-08T17:00:00-05:00">February 8, 1932—5
                        p.m.</date></dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>46. Your 184, February 3, 11 a.m., and 210, February 8, 3 p.m., in regard to the
                    situation at Hankow.</p>
                <list>
                    <label>1.</label>
                    <item>Department approves the instructions which have been sent to Hankow by the
                        Legation and by the Minister as reported in your 210, February 8, 3
                        p.m.</item>
                    <label>2.</label>
                    <item>Keep Department informed in regard to developments. Repeat to
                        Minister.</item>
                </list>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Stimson</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
